  "worked_solution": "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2\\pi x)=-1\n$$\n\n are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\pi x & =\\pi +2n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =1+2n \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}+n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx=\\pm \\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm \\frac{3}{2},\\,\\pm \\frac{5}{2},\\,\u2026\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA={\\pm \\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm \\frac{3}{2},\\,\\pm \\frac{5}{2},\\,\u2026}.\n$$",
